# 🔑 Authentication Flow

## Registration

```
Register

↓

Create User

↓

Generate Verification Token

↓

Hash Token

↓

Store Token

↓

Send Verification Email
```

---

## Login

```
Validate Credentials

↓

Verify Email

↓

Generate Access Token (RS256)

↓

Generate Refresh Token (HS256)

↓

Hash Refresh Token

↓

Store Session

↓

Return Access Token
```

---

## Refresh Token Flow

```
Refresh Token

↓

Verify JWT

↓

Find Session (JTI)

↓

Compare Hash

↓

Delete Old Session

↓

Generate New Refresh Token

↓

Store New Session

↓

Return New Tokens
```

---

## Password Reset

```
Forgot Password

↓

Generate Secure Token

↓

Hash Token

↓

Store Token

↓

Send Email

↓

Verify Token

↓

Update Password

↓

Delete All Sessions
```

---

# 🔒 Security Design

## Access Tokens

- RS256
- 15 minute expiry
- Contains:
  - User ID
  - User Role

Only the Auth Service owns the **private key**.

Future microservices (API Gateway, Chat Service, etc.) verify tokens using the **public key**.

---

## Refresh Tokens

- HS256
- 7 day expiry
- Stored as bcrypt hashes
- Rotation on every refresh
- One session per refresh token

---

## Device Sessions

Each login creates an independent session.

Stored information:

- Session ID
- JTI
- User Agent
- IP Address
- Creation Time
- Expiry Time

Supports:

- Logout Current Device
- Logout Specific Device
- Logout All Devices

---

