# API Endpoints

## Authentication

| Method | Endpoint       |
| ------ | -------------- |
| POST   | /auth/register |
| POST   | /auth/login    |
| POST   | /auth/logout   |
| POST   | /auth/refresh  |

---

## Email Verification

| Method | Endpoint           |
| ------ | ------------------ |
| GET    | /auth/verify-email |

---

## Password

| Method | Endpoint              |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| POST   | /auth/forgot-password |
| POST   | /auth/reset-password  |

---

## Sessions

| Method | Endpoint     |
| ------ | ------------ |
| GET    | /session     |
| DELETE | /session/:id |
| DELETE | /session     |

---

# Environment Variables

```env
DATABASE_URL=

PORT=

ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY=

REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=

EMAIL_USER=

EMAIL_PASS=
```

RSA keys are generated locally and are **not committed**.

```
keys/
├── private.pem
└── public.pem
```

---

# Why This Project?

This project is designed as the authentication component of a future distributed backend system.

Rather than acting as a standalone authentication API, it serves as an **Identity Provider** responsible for issuing secure JWTs that can be trusted across multiple independent services.
